<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-morphogen-hypothesis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-morphogen-hypothesis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reaction-diffusion of morphogens accounts for biological pattern" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-morphogen-hypothesis> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Chemical substances that react and diffuse through tissue (morphogens) are sufficient to account for the main phenomena of morphogenesis." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-morphogen-hypothesis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-morphogen-hypothesis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "no canonical formalization: the claim asserts that a biological pattern is generated by a system of the form u_t = F(u) + D\\nabla^2 u with D not proportional to the identity" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-morphogen-hypothesis> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Formal status: a framework rather than a mathematical proposition. Kondo and Asai (1995) confirmed the predicted stripe-branching dynamics in Pomacanthus and Castets et al. (1990) produced Turing patterns chemically. Mechanical buckling, prepatterns and cell-cell signalling can produce the same patterns, so a matching pattern alone does not identify the mechanism." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-morphogen-hypothesis> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "In a candidate system, identify the interacting molecules, measure their kinetics and diffusion, and confirm novel predictions such as stripe insertion during growth or pattern change after a targeted perturbation, while ruling out mechanical alternatives." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-morphogen-hypothesis> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "principle-or-framework" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-morphogen-hypothesis> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Alan Turing (1952) The chemical basis of morphogenesis" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-morphogen-hypothesis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1038/376765a0> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-morphogen-hypothesis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.64.2953> .
}
